{"cid": "UgwVulEUEvNd8RvbvBh4AaABAg", "text": "At a ham radio junk sale in Eastbourne in the eighties, a box of HUGE old vintage caps came up for auction (they were about 6” long and 2” diameter). Someone in the audience asked if they had been discharged: A guy gingerly selected one, then took a damp paperback book and bridged the terminals with it. Massive sizzle and a loud bang, accompanied by lots of magic smoke. Ever since that time, I’ve been VERY wary of big Cs…", "time": "10 months ago", "author": "@sihartgroves7549", "channel": "UCj4ypVVBtghjjN8LNFN7upg", "votes": "1", "replies": "2", "photo": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_mVmJB1GqgrD0zkQHoN1-BtS4gosFSM7ia4e046-w84pdw=s88-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj", "heart": false, "reply": false, "time_parsed": 1740782144.142255}
